What does the following snippet print to standard output?

```java
class CallbackListener {
    int registeredId;
    void register(Dispatcher d) {
        d.attach(this);
    }
}
class Dispatcher {
    int capturedId = 99;
    void attach(CallbackListener listener) {
        listener.registeredId = 77;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        CallbackListener item = new CallbackListener();
        Dispatcher dispatcher = new Dispatcher();
        item.register(dispatcher);
        System.out.println(item.registeredId);
    }
}
```

Evaluate the following inner class instance reference code. What is output?

```java
class EnclosingScope {
    int scale = 100;
    class NestedWorker {
        int scale = 20;
        void process() {
            System.out.print(this.scale + " ");
            System.out.print(EnclosingScope.this.scale);
        }
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        EnclosingScope outer = new EnclosingScope();
        EnclosingScope.NestedWorker worker = outer.new NestedWorker();
        worker.process();
    }
}
```
